#N Langton's loop
#C The initial configuration of Langton's self-reproducing loop (1984): a
#C sheathed loop of 85 cells carrying the instruction sequence that extrudes
#C an arm, grows it, turns it four times and closes it into a daughter. The
#C first daughter is complete at about generation 150.
#C Transcribed data, not constructed here; see rules/langtons-loops.rule.
x = 14, y = 10, rule = langtons-loops
